  "scope": "Commuting ancillary energy records fail for incompatible positive local terms. A quantum prefix-clock connection repairs the noncommuting source problem and represents the supplied total Hamiltonian at its final clock. A small-chart nearest-neighbor locality estimate, an exact finite-register realization, and spectrally rounded finite encodings of general prefix Hamiltonians are checked. The rounded dynamics approximate supplied dynamics with an explicit error; the encoding does not select that Hamiltonian. No uniformly local finite-spin gravitational phase, Einstein deformation algebra, universal coupling, Standard Model dynamics, or TOE is proved. No Lean theorem."
